{
 "elemod": 2,
 "id": "tonefx",
 "version": "3.2a3",
 "title": "Tone+FX",
 "description": "Tone+FX 3.2a by Digital Alchemy DSP (github.com/DigiAlchemydsp/RingTone), ported from its original FM-groovebox version: a master effect suite on every output: main, headphones and USB. Master ring modulator, a low-shelf/high-shelf master EQ (TILT), a Crunch/Redux lo-fi stage (BITS / SR / CRUNCH), a wavefolder with a continuous CLEAN/MUD/DIST/TRSH fold type, a five-mode modulation insert (PITCH: WOB / SHFT, STEREO: FLAN / PAN / WIDE), an output meter and a soft output ceiling. Seven pages after the stock master pages (FUNC+LFO; LEFT/RIGHT rotate the pages): DIGI RING, FOLD, TILT, CRUSH, PITCH, STEREO and PERFORM. PERFORM is reached with UP from any of the six: the eight knobs set one depth per FX block, and the 16 trigs are momentary performance pads (four blocks of four intensities: ring / fold+crush / pitch / pan) that ramp their block up while held and back on release. Settings follow the pattern while the unit is on (they are not saved over a power cycle on the DT1), and the FX answer incoming MIDI CC. The unit starts with its own intro (no boot splash).",
 "category": "Sound",
 "author": "Digital Alchemy DSP (DT1 port: gdeo607)",
 "license": "GPL-2.0-or-later",
 "target": {
  "device": "digitakt-mk1",
  "product": "Digitakt mk1",
  "os": "1.54",
  "syx_sha256": "f78ba80fa7b1da5fb0e1ff61ad61e9e71aafe79f4364fc49679f3651353e3cf6",
